Subject: cli: leave flushing stdout to stdio on OpenVMS

The CLI SAPI flushes stdout after every piece of output (implicit_flush is
always on in the CLI).  On OpenVMS each fflush() of SYS$OUTPUT ends a
record, so `var_dump("UTC")` printed `string(3) "`, `UTC` and `"` on three
lines (vms-php PORTING_LOG #19, #20).  On VMS the flush handler leaves it
to stdio, which ends records at newlines and flushes at exit.
---
--- a/sapi/cli/php_cli.c
+++ b/sapi/cli/php_cli.c
@@ -299,6 +299,13 @@
 
 static void sapi_cli_flush(void *server_context) /* {{{ */
 {
+#ifdef __VMS
+	/* Every fflush() of SYS$OUTPUT ends a record on OpenVMS, and the CLI flushes
+	 * after each piece of output (implicit_flush), so var_dump()'s pieces came
+	 * out as separate lines.  stdio ends records at newlines and flushes at
+	 * exit, so leave it to stdio. */
+	return;
+#endif
 	/* Ignore EBADF here, it's caused by the fact that STDIN/STDOUT/STDERR streams
 	 * are/could be closed before fflush() is called.
 	 */
